From d773cf3213b42b9ba84c0a6bc367d7f03fbcd848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds <port@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:44:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: re-pin the MSL new producer debug-line shapes after
 1519

Patch 1519 added #ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS lines to src/to91_msl_scalar_new.cpp
and src/to91_msl_array_new.cpp. The DS build does not define the macro, so
the selected code is unchanged, but the physical source line numbers shift
and MWCC writes different .debug_info/.debug_line sections and a different
.dwarf_line symbol in the retained raw compiler product.

Verified: comparing the pinned shape with the tool's own shape.inventory()
over the current compiler-full objects shows differences in exactly
.debug_info (payload hash), .debug_line (record/payload hash) and one
.dwarf_line.* symbol size (36 -> 48 for .debug_line, 226 -> 238 section
length). Every allocated/executable section is identical, and the tool's
producer profile still asserts the code function sizes and payloads.

Regenerated with tools/msl-new-partition/shape.py (not edited by hand), as
the gate documentation requires. profile.json pins the two fixtures
themselves as modules, so their new hashes are re-pinned in the same patch.
